                                          Assignment: Enhance Wrangler with Byte Size and Time Duration Units Parsers 
1. Objective: 
           Introduce support for BYTE_SIZE and TIME_DURATION tokens in Wrangler to simplify handling units 
           like KB, MB, ms, s, etc., and create an aggregation directive that uses them. 
2. Grammar Modifications (Directives.g4) 
     Changes Made: 
           Added lexer rules: 
              o BYTE_SIZE 
              o TIME_DURATION 
            Added parser rules: 
              o byteSize 
              o timeDurationfh 
             Updated the value rule to accept these new types. 
Purpose: 
To enable recipes like: 
aggregate-stats :col_size :col_time total_size total_time 
which use values like "10KB" or "150ms". 
3. API Changes (wrangler-api module) 
Files Added: 
     ByteSize.java 
     TimeDuration.java 
Class Responsibilities: 
  Extend Token.java 
   Parse string tokens (e.g., "10MB" or "5s") 
   Provide canonical unit methods: 
     o long getBytes() for ByteSize 
     o long getNanoseconds() for TimeDuration 
4. Token Type Enhancements 
Updates Made: 
    TokenType.java: 
          o Added BYTE_SIZE and TIME_DURATION 
   UsageDefinition: 
        o Updated to accept these new types in directives 
5. New Directive (wrangler-core module) 
   Class Created: 
          AggregateStats.java 
    Implements: 
       Directive interface 
Takes Arguments: 
          1. sizeColumn – Byte size column name 
          2. timeColumn – Time duration column name 
           3. outputSizeColumn – Output for total size in MB 
           4. outputTimeColumn – Output for total time in seconds 
Execution Flow: 
              Iterates through rows 
              Converts and sums byte sizes and durations 
              Returns a single aggregated Row with converted values 
6. Parser Visitor Updates 
    Modified Visitor: 
            TokenGroupVisitor.java or equivalent 
    Additions: 
            Logic to visit and handle BYTE_SIZE and TIME_DURATION tokens 
            Added them into the TokenGroup for execution 
7. Unit Testing 
         Added in wrangler-core: 
                Tested Classes: 
                  o ByteSizeTest.java 
                  o TimeDurationTest.java 
                  o AggregateStatsTest.java
 
Test Coverage Includes: 
       Valid and invalid parsing inputs (10kb, 1.5MB, 5ms, 2.1s) 
        Aggregation logic correctness using TestingRig.execute(recipe, rows) 
        Output assertion: 
            Assert.assertEquals(expectedTotalSize, row.getValue("total_size_mb"), 0.001); 
            Assert.assertEquals(expectedTotalTime, row.getValue("total_time_sec"), 0.001); 
8. Execution & Build Info 
mvn clean install 
